    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-7",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "7 Tribunal may request assistance",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-7"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.20",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A request by a Tribunal, for assistance that it needs to perform its\nfunctions in respect of an investigation or prosecution it is\nconducting or proposes to conduct, is to be made to the\nAttorney-General, or a person authorised by the Attorney-General.\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), the request may be for assistance\nof one or more of the following types:\n(a) arresting and surrendering to the Tribunal a person in relation\nto whom the Tribunal has issued an arrest warrant;\n(b) executing a request for search and seizure;\n(c) obtaining evidence, a document or other article;\n(d) providing a document or other record;\n(e) locating and identifying a witness or suspect;\n(f) arranging for a person to give evidence or assist an\ninvestigation;\n(g) causing the forfeiture of property or the proceeds of crime;\n(h) serving documents;\n(i) arranging for the Tribunal to sit in Australia.\n(3) If a request by a Tribunal is made to, or received by, a person\nauthorised under subsection (1), the request is taken for the\npurposes of this Act to have been made to, or received by, the\nAttorney-General.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A request by a Tribunal, for assistance that it needs to perform its\nfunctions in respect of an investigation or prosecution it is\nconducting or proposes to conduct, is to be made to the\nAttorney-General, or a person authorised by the Attorney-General.\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), the request may be for assistance\nof one or more of the following types:\n(a) arresting and surrendering to the Tribunal a person in relation\nto whom the Tribunal has issued an arrest warrant;\n(b) executing a request for search and seizure;\n(c) obtaining evidence, a document or other article;\n(d) providing a document or other record;\n(e) locating and identifying a witness or suspect;\n(f) arranging for a person to give evidence or assist an\ninvestigation;\n(g) causing the forfeiture of property or the proceeds of crime;\n(h) serving documents;\n(i) arranging for the Tribunal to sit in Australia.\n(3) If a request by a Tribunal is made to, or received by, a person\nauthorised under subsection (1), the request is taken for the\npurposes of this Act to have been made to, or received by, the\nAttorney-General.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-7-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-7-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-7-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "46d9bf8bd057e95437c7cfbf31e9f9d545e91c7bb224639a9e7c98c6d957f836"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-7",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "7 Tribunal may request assistance",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 20,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A request by a Tribunal, for assistance that it needs to perform its\nfunctions in respect of an investigation or prosecution it is\nconducting or proposes to conduct, is to be made to the\nAttorney-General, or a person authorised by the Attorney-General.\n(2) Without limiting subsection (1), the request may be for assistance\nof one or more of the following types:\n(a) arresting and surrendering to the Tribunal a person in relation\nto whom the Tribunal has issued an arrest warrant;\n(b) executing a request for search and seizure;\n(c) obtaining evidence, a document or other article;\n(d) providing a document or other record;\n(e) locating and identifying a witness or suspect;\n(f) arranging for a person to give evidence or assist an\ninvestigation;\n(g) causing the forfeiture of property or the proceeds of crime;\n(h) serving documents;\n(i) arranging for the Tribunal to sit in Australia.\n(3) If a request by a Tribunal is made to, or received by, a person\nauthorised under subsection (1), the request is taken for the\npurposes of this Act to have been made to, or received by, the\nAttorney-General."
    },
