    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-10",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "10 Issue of warrants",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-10"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.22",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A magistrate must issue a warrant, in the statutory form, for a\nperson’s arrest if an application is made, in the statutory form, on\nbehalf of the Tribunal, for issue of a warrant pursuant to the notice.\n(2) A magistrate must issue a warrant, in the statutory form, for a\nperson’s arrest if:\n(a) an application is made, in the statutory form, on behalf of a\nTribunal, for issue of a warrant otherwise than pursuant to\nsuch a notice; and\n(b) the application is accompanied by a copy of an arrest warrant\nfor the person that was issued by the Tribunal; and\n(c) the application contains a statement to the effect that, because\nof circumstances of urgency, it is necessary to issue a warrant\n\n\nSurrender of persons to a Tribunal  Part 3\nArrest of persons  Division 1\nSection 11\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nCompilation date: 28/03/2026\nbefore receiving a notice from the Attorney-General under\nsection 9.\n(3) The magistrate must without delay send to the Attorney-General a\nreport stating whether the magistrate has issued the warrant. Note:\nDivision 4 of Part 7 deals with matters relating to arrest.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A magistrate must issue a warrant, in the statutory form, for a\nperson’s arrest if an application is made, in the statutory form, on\nbehalf of the Tribunal, for issue of a warrant pursuant to the notice.\n(2) A magistrate must issue a warrant, in the statutory form, for a\nperson’s arrest if:\n(a) an application is made, in the statutory form, on behalf of a\nTribunal, for issue of a warrant otherwise than pursuant to\nsuch a notice; and\n(b) the application is accompanied by a copy of an arrest warrant\nfor the person that was issued by the Tribunal; and\n(c) the application contains a statement to the effect that, because\nof circumstances of urgency, it is necessary to issue a warrant\n\n\nSurrender of persons to a Tribunal  Part 3\nArrest of persons  Division 1\nSection 11\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nCompilation date: 28/03/2026\nbefore receiving a notice from the Attorney-General under\nsection 9.\n(3) The magistrate must without delay send to the Attorney-General a\nreport stating whether the magistrate has issued the warrant. Note:\nDivision 4 of Part 7 deals with matters relating to arrest.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-10-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-10-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-10-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e1df8047b7925ed24100887b299076a4ec95e98dddb43571ba36f6dad720eece"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-10",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "10 Issue of warrants",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 22,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A magistrate must issue a warrant, in the statutory form, for a\nperson’s arrest if an application is made, in the statutory form, on\nbehalf of the Tribunal, for issue of a warrant pursuant to the notice.\n(2) A magistrate must issue a warrant, in the statutory form, for a\nperson’s arrest if:\n(a) an application is made, in the statutory form, on behalf of a\nTribunal, for issue of a warrant otherwise than pursuant to\nsuch a notice; and\n(b) the application is accompanied by a copy of an arrest warrant\nfor the person that was issued by the Tribunal; and\n(c) the application contains a statement to the effect that, because\nof circumstances of urgency, it is necessary to issue a warrant\n\n\nSurrender of persons to a Tribunal  Part 3\nArrest of persons  Division 1\nSection 11\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nCompilation date: 28/03/2026\nbefore receiving a notice from the Attorney-General under\nsection 9.\n(3) The magistrate must without delay send to the Attorney-General a\nreport stating whether the magistrate has issued the warrant. Note:\nDivision 4 of Part 7 deals with matters relating to arrest."
    },
