    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-15",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "15 Application for search warrants",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-15"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.25",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n(a) a person is arrested under a warrant issued under section 10;\nand\n(b) a police officer has reasonable grounds for suspecting that\nevidential material relating to a Tribunal offence in respect of\nwhich the warrant was issued is, or within the applicable\nperiod referred to in subsection (3) of this section will be, at\nany premises;\nthe police officer may, by an information on oath that sets out the\ngrounds for that suspicion, apply for a search warrant in relation to\nthe premises to search for that material.\n(2) If:\n(a) a person is arrested under a warrant issued under section 10;\nand",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If:\n(a) a person is arrested under a warrant issued under section 10;\nand\n(b) a police officer has reasonable grounds for suspecting that\nevidential material relating to a Tribunal offence in respect of\nwhich the warrant was issued is, or within the applicable\nperiod referred to in subsection (3) of this section will be, at\nany premises;\nthe police officer may, by an information on oath that sets out the\ngrounds for that suspicion, apply for a search warrant in relation to\nthe premises to search for that material.\n(2) If:\n(a) a person is arrested under a warrant issued under section 10;\nand",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-15-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-15-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "a568be2487a679203052026e99a5fcb21007f6b3c9711821cc41bbdfeb25c025"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-15",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15 Application for search warrants",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 25,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n(a) a person is arrested under a warrant issued under section 10;\nand\n(b) a police officer has reasonable grounds for suspecting that\nevidential material relating to a Tribunal offence in respect of\nwhich the warrant was issued is, or within the applicable\nperiod referred to in subsection (3) of this section will be, at\nany premises;\nthe police officer may, by an information on oath that sets out the\ngrounds for that suspicion, apply for a search warrant in relation to\nthe premises to search for that material.\n(2) If:\n(a) a person is arrested under a warrant issued under section 10;\nand"
    },
