      "skos:note": "Police officer may apply for search warrant to search premises for evidential material."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-15-ss-1",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "15(1) Application for search warrants",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 25,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If:\n(a) a person is arrested under a warrant issued under section 10;\nand\n(b) a police officer has reasonable grounds for suspecting that\nevidential material relating to a Tribunal offence in respect of\nwhich the warrant was issued is, or within the applicable\nperiod referred to in subsection (3) of this section will be, at\nany premises;\nthe police officer may, by an information on oath that sets out the\ngrounds for that suspicion, apply for a search warrant in relation to\nthe premises to search for that material."
    },
