    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-16",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "16 Surrender determination by Attorney-General",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-16"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.27",
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General must determine whether a person remanded\nunder Division 1 is to be surrendered to the Tribunal that sought\nthe arrest of the person under that Division.\n(2) Unless the Attorney-General is satisfied that there are special\ncircumstances, he or she must determine that the person is to be\nsurrendered to the Tribunal.\n(3) In considering whether there are special circumstances, the\nAttorney-General must:\n(a) give the person a reasonable opportunity to provide to the\nAttorney-General documents intended to show that there are\nspecial circumstances; and\n(b) consider any documents so provided.\n(4) The determination must be made as soon as reasonably practicable,\nhaving regard to the circumstances, after the person is remanded\nunder Division 1.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) The Attorney-General must determine whether a person remanded\nunder Division 1 is to be surrendered to the Tribunal that sought\nthe arrest of the person under that Division.\n(2) Unless the Attorney-General is satisfied that there are special\ncircumstances, he or she must determine that the person is to be\nsurrendered to the Tribunal.\n(3) In considering whether there are special circumstances, the\nAttorney-General must:\n(a) give the person a reasonable opportunity to provide to the\nAttorney-General documents intended to show that there are\nspecial circumstances; and\n(b) consider any documents so provided.\n(4) The determination must be made as soon as reasonably practicable,\nhaving regard to the circumstances, after the person is remanded\nunder Division 1.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-16-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-16-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-16-ss-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-16-ss-4"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "981437692aea58059c70d484560447dc2426e8ea785f169b36104b06bbf67143"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-16",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "16 Surrender determination by Attorney-General",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 27,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General must determine whether a person remanded\nunder Division 1 is to be surrendered to the Tribunal that sought\nthe arrest of the person under that Division.\n(2) Unless the Attorney-General is satisfied that there are special\ncircumstances, he or she must determine that the person is to be\nsurrendered to the Tribunal.\n(3) In considering whether there are special circumstances, the\nAttorney-General must:\n(a) give the person a reasonable opportunity to provide to the\nAttorney-General documents intended to show that there are\nspecial circumstances; and\n(b) consider any documents so provided.\n(4) The determination must be made as soon as reasonably practicable,\nhaving regard to the circumstances, after the person is remanded\nunder Division 1."
    },
