    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-20",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "20 Detention following surrender warrants",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-20"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.28",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Attorney-General issues the surrender warrant, the person\nmust be brought as soon as practicable before a magistrate in the\nState or Territory in which the person is on remand.\n\n\nSurrender of persons to a Tribunal  Part 3\nSurrender of persons  Division 2\nSection 21\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nCompilation date: 28/03/2026\n(2) A magistrate must remand the person in custody for such period or\nperiods as may be necessary to enable the warrant to be executed.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the Attorney-General issues the surrender warrant, the person\nmust be brought as soon as practicable before a magistrate in the\nState or Territory in which the person is on remand.\n\n\nSurrender of persons to a Tribunal  Part 3\nSurrender of persons  Division 2\nSection 21\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nCompilation date: 28/03/2026\n(2) A magistrate must remand the person in custody for such period or\nperiods as may be necessary to enable the warrant to be executed.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-20-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-20-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "fa7fb558b517f25a376478a673bbc3cea193c2a4e633d2c72fba424697a1a453"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-20",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "20 Detention following surrender warrants",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 28,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Attorney-General issues the surrender warrant, the person\nmust be brought as soon as practicable before a magistrate in the\nState or Territory in which the person is on remand.\n\n\nSurrender of persons to a Tribunal  Part 3\nSurrender of persons  Division 2\nSection 21\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nCompilation date: 28/03/2026\n(2) A magistrate must remand the person in custody for such period or\nperiods as may be necessary to enable the warrant to be executed."
    },
