    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-21",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21 Content of surrender warrants",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-21"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.29",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A surrender warrant in relation to the person (the eligible person)\nmust:\n(a) require the person in whose custody the eligible person is\nbeing held to release the eligible person into the custody of a\npolice officer; and\n(b) authorise the police officer to transport the eligible person in\ncustody, and, if necessary or convenient, to detain the eligible\nperson in custody, for the purpose of enabling the eligible\nperson:\n(i) to be placed in the custody of a specified person who is\nan officer of the Tribunal or other person authorised by\nthe Tribunal; and\n(ii) to be transported to a place specified by the Tribunal;\nand\n(c) authorise the specified person to transport the eligible person\nin custody to a place specified by the Tribunal for the\npurpose of surrendering the eligible person to a person\nappointed by the Tribunal to receive the person.\n(2) A place referred to in paragraph (1)(b) or (c) may be a place in or\noutside Australia.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A surrender warrant in relation to the person (the eligible person)\nmust:\n(a) require the person in whose custody the eligible person is\nbeing held to release the eligible person into the custody of a\npolice officer; and\n(b) authorise the police officer to transport the eligible person in\ncustody, and, if necessary or convenient, to detain the eligible\nperson in custody, for the purpose of enabling the eligible\nperson:\n(i) to be placed in the custody of a specified person who is\nan officer of the Tribunal or other person authorised by\nthe Tribunal; and\n(ii) to be transported to a place specified by the Tribunal;\nand\n(c) authorise the specified person to transport the eligible person\nin custody to a place specified by the Tribunal for the\npurpose of surrendering the eligible person to a person\nappointed by the Tribunal to receive the person.\n(2) A place referred to in paragraph (1)(b) or (c) may be a place in or\noutside Australia.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-21-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-21-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4075caca5a5c6c791664ae6baab5397b94e615faffc150cc7bab39ebadfd6b4c"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-21",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "21 Content of surrender warrants",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 29,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A surrender warrant in relation to the person (the eligible person)\nmust:\n(a) require the person in whose custody the eligible person is\nbeing held to release the eligible person into the custody of a\npolice officer; and\n(b) authorise the police officer to transport the eligible person in\ncustody, and, if necessary or convenient, to detain the eligible\nperson in custody, for the purpose of enabling the eligible\nperson:\n(i) to be placed in the custody of a specified person who is\nan officer of the Tribunal or other person authorised by\nthe Tribunal; and\n(ii) to be transported to a place specified by the Tribunal;\nand\n(c) authorise the specified person to transport the eligible person\nin custody to a place specified by the Tribunal for the\npurpose of surrendering the eligible person to a person\nappointed by the Tribunal to receive the person.\n(2) A place referred to in paragraph (1)(b) or (c) may be a place in or\noutside Australia."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-21-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "21(1) Content of surrender warrants",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-21-ss-1"
      },
