      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 29,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A surrender warrant in relation to the person (the eligible person)\nmust:\n(a) require the person in whose custody the eligible person is\nbeing held to release the eligible person into the custody of a\npolice officer; and\n(b) authorise the police officer to transport the eligible person in\ncustody, and, if necessary or convenient, to detain the eligible\nperson in custody, for the purpose of enabling the eligible\nperson:\n(i) to be placed in the custody of a specified person who is\nan officer of the Tribunal or other person authorised by\nthe Tribunal; and\n(ii) to be transported to a place specified by the Tribunal;\nand\n(c) authorise the specified person to transport the eligible person\nin custody to a place specified by the Tribunal for the\npurpose of surrendering the eligible person to a person\nappointed by the Tribunal to receive the person."
    },
