    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-24",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "24 Effect of surrender to Tribunal on person’s terms of",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-24"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.30",
      "values:originalText": "imprisonment\n(1) If, at the time a person was surrendered to a Tribunal under this\nPart in connection with a Tribunal offence, the person was serving\na sentence of imprisonment in respect of an offence against a law\nof the Commonwealth or of a Territory, or was otherwise subject to\ndetention under a law of the Commonwealth or of a Territory:\n(a) any time spent by the person in custody in connection with\nthe surrender warrant; and\n(b) subject to subsection (2), any time spent by the person in\ncustody in connection with detention by, or on the order of,\nthe Tribunal in respect of the Tribunal offence;\nis to be counted as time served towards the sentence of\nimprisonment or period of detention.\n(2) If the person is convicted of the Tribunal offence, time spent by the\nperson in custody serving a sentence of imprisonment imposed by\n\n\nSurrender of persons to a Tribunal  Part 3\nSurrender of persons  Division 2\nSection 25\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nCompilation date: 28/03/2026\nthe Tribunal for the Tribunal offence is not to be counted as time\ntowards the sentence of imprisonment or period of detention\nreferred to in subsection (1).\n(3) A reference in this section to time spent in custody includes a\nreference to time spent in custody outside Australia.",
      "skos:definition": "imprisonment\n(1) If, at the time a person was surrendered to a Tribunal under this\nPart in connection with a Tribunal offence, the person was serving\na sentence of imprisonment in respect of an offence against a law\nof the Commonwealth or of a Territory, or was otherwise subject to\ndetention under a law of the Commonwealth or of a Territory:\n(a) any time spent by the person in custody in connection with\nthe surrender warrant; and\n(b) subject to subsection (2), any time spent by the person in\ncustody in connection with detention by, or on the order of,\nthe Tribunal in respect of the Tribunal offence;\nis to be counted as time served towards the sentence of\nimprisonment or period of detention.\n(2) If the person is convicted of the Tribunal offence, time spent by the\nperson in custody serving a sentence of imprisonment imposed by\n\n\nSurrender of persons to a Tribunal  Part 3\nSurrender of persons  Division 2\nSection 25\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nCompilation date: 28/03/2026\nthe Tribunal for the Tribunal offence is not to be counted as time\ntowards the sentence of imprisonment or period of detention\nreferred to in subsection (1).\n(3) A reference in this section to time spent in custody includes a\nreference to time spent in custody outside Australia.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-24-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-24-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-24-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "bc1b7d6e393af40d2377f78f818b40f7244006d753d0672907bad8f25a8e7d51"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-24",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "24 Effect of surrender to Tribunal on person’s terms of",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 30,
      "values:originalText": "imprisonment\n(1) If, at the time a person was surrendered to a Tribunal under this\nPart in connection with a Tribunal offence, the person was serving\na sentence of imprisonment in respect of an offence against a law\nof the Commonwealth or of a Territory, or was otherwise subject to\ndetention under a law of the Commonwealth or of a Territory:\n(a) any time spent by the person in custody in connection with\nthe surrender warrant; and\n(b) subject to subsection (2), any time spent by the person in\ncustody in connection with detention by, or on the order of,\nthe Tribunal in respect of the Tribunal offence;\nis to be counted as time served towards the sentence of\nimprisonment or period of detention.\n(2) If the person is convicted of the Tribunal offence, time spent by the\nperson in custody serving a sentence of imprisonment imposed by\n\n\nSurrender of persons to a Tribunal  Part 3\nSurrender of persons  Division 2\nSection 25\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nCompilation date: 28/03/2026\nthe Tribunal for the Tribunal offence is not to be counted as time\ntowards the sentence of imprisonment or period of detention\nreferred to in subsection (1).\n(3) A reference in this section to time spent in custody includes a\nreference to time spent in custody outside Australia."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-24-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "24(1) Effect of surrender to Tribunal on person’s terms of",
