    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-28-2",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "28 Producing documents or other articles",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-28-2"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.34",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Attorney-General authorises production of documents or\nother articles, a magistrate may require production of the\ndocuments or other articles.\n(2) Subject to subsection (3), if the documents or other articles are\nproduced, a magistrate must send them to the Attorney-General\ntogether with a written statement certifying that they were\nproduced to that magistrate.\n(3) In the case of documents, a magistrate may send to the\nAttorney-General copies of the documents certified by that\nmagistrate to be true copies.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If the Attorney-General authorises production of documents or\nother articles, a magistrate may require production of the\ndocuments or other articles.\n(2) Subject to subsection (3), if the documents or other articles are\nproduced, a magistrate must send them to the Attorney-General\ntogether with a written statement certifying that they were\nproduced to that magistrate.\n(3) In the case of documents, a magistrate may send to the\nAttorney-General copies of the documents certified by that\nmagistrate to be true copies.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-28-2-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-28-2-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-28-2-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "56d6cdd57668e217f7c7eb64a44623717840d17e1a0b1e15b2b9a92fb940f3ff"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-28-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "28 Producing documents or other articles",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 34,
      "values:originalText": "(1) If the Attorney-General authorises production of documents or\nother articles, a magistrate may require production of the\ndocuments or other articles.\n(2) Subject to subsection (3), if the documents or other articles are\nproduced, a magistrate must send them to the Attorney-General\ntogether with a written statement certifying that they were\nproduced to that magistrate.\n(3) In the case of documents, a magistrate may send to the\nAttorney-General copies of the documents certified by that\nmagistrate to be true copies."
    },
