    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-29-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "29(3) Legal representation",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-29-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.34",
      "values:originalText": "(3) If the Tribunal so requests, the Magistrate conducting a proceeding\nunder section 27 or 28 (or both) may permit examination or\ncross-examination of a person giving evidence or producing a\ndocument or other article at the proceeding, by:\n\n\nOther forms of assistance to a Tribunal  Part 4\nTaking evidence etc.  Division 1\nSection 30\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nCompilation date: 28/03/2026\n(a) the person to whom the proceeding before, or the\ninvestigation conducted by, the Tribunal relates; or\n(b) that person’s legal representative; or\n(c) the Tribunal’s legal representative;\nthrough a video link.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) If the Tribunal so requests, the Magistrate conducting a proceeding\nunder section 27 or 28 (or both) may permit examination or\ncross-examination of a person giving evidence or producing a\ndocument or other article at the proceeding, by:\n\n\nOther forms of assistance to a Tribunal  Part 4\nTaking evidence etc.  Division 1\nSection 30\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nCompilation date: 28/03/2026\n(a) the person to whom the proceeding before, or the\ninvestigation conducted by, the Tribunal relates; or\n(b) that person’s legal representative; or\n(c) the Tribunal’s legal representative;\nthrough a video link.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-29"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-29-ss-3-norm"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "315b9692252903887a75c3683e7ee4dd02e4d3d8ab6986fef6aa3fe022d4a30f",
      "skos:note": "Allow examination or cross-examination via video link."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-29-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "29(3) Legal representation",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 34,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If the Tribunal so requests, the Magistrate conducting a proceeding\nunder section 27 or 28 (or both) may permit examination or\ncross-examination of a person giving evidence or producing a\ndocument or other article at the proceeding, by:\n\n\nOther forms of assistance to a Tribunal  Part 4\nTaking evidence etc.  Division 1\nSection 30\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nCompilation date: 28/03/2026\n(a) the person to whom the proceeding before, or the\ninvestigation conducted by, the Tribunal relates; or\n(b) that person’s legal representative; or\n(c) the Tribunal’s legal representative;\nthrough a video link."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-29-ss-3-norm",
