    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-30",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "30 Form of certificates",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-30"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.35",
      "values:originalText": "A certificate by a magistrate under subsection 27(2) or 28(2) must\nstate whether, when the evidence was taken or the documents or\nother articles were produced, any of the following persons were\npresent:\n(a) the person to whom the proceeding before, or the\ninvestigation conducted by, the Tribunal relates, or his or her\nlegal representative (if any);\n(b) any other person giving evidence or producing documents or\nother articles, or his or her legal representative (if any).\n31  Compellability of persons to attend etc.\n(1) Subject to subsections (2) and (3), the laws of each State or\nTerritory with respect to compelling persons:\n(a) to attend before a magistrate; and\n(b) to give evidence, answer questions, and produce documents\nor other articles;\non the hearing of a charge against a person for an offence against\nthe law of that State or Territory apply, so far as they are capable\nof application, with respect to so compelling persons for the\npurposes of this Division.",
      "skos:definition": "A certificate by a magistrate under subsection 27(2) or 28(2) must\nstate whether, when the evidence was taken or the documents or\nother articles were produced, any of the following persons were\npresent:\n(a) the person to whom the proceeding before, or the\ninvestigation conducted by, the Tribunal relates, or his or her\nlegal representative (if any);\n(b) any other person giving evidence or producing documents or\nother articles, or his or her legal representative (if any).\n31  Compellability of persons to attend etc.\n(1) Subject to subsections (2) and (3), the laws of each State or\nTerritory with respect to compelling persons:\n(a) to attend before a magistrate; and\n(b) to give evidence, answer questions, and produce documents\nor other articles;\non the hearing of a charge against a person for an offence against\nthe law of that State or Territory apply, so far as they are capable\nof application, with respect to so compelling persons for the\npurposes of this Division.",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-30-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-30-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "1f5a51dc6de026d12770f09586d4d7688523032c029e33b135f013345c79d0c6",
      "skos:note": "Must state presence of certain persons",
      "dc:description": "Yes"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-30",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "30 Form of certificates",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 35,
      "values:originalText": "A certificate by a magistrate under subsection 27(2) or 28(2) must\nstate whether, when the evidence was taken or the documents or\nother articles were produced, any of the following persons were\npresent:\n(a) the person to whom the proceeding before, or the\ninvestigation conducted by, the Tribunal relates, or his or her\nlegal representative (if any);\n(b) any other person giving evidence or producing documents or\nother articles, or his or her legal representative (if any).\n31  Compellability of persons to attend etc.\n(1) Subject to subsections (2) and (3), the laws of each State or\nTerritory with respect to compelling persons:\n(a) to attend before a magistrate; and\n(b) to give evidence, answer questions, and produce documents\nor other articles;\non the hearing of a charge against a person for an offence against\nthe law of that State or Territory apply, so far as they are capable\nof application, with respect to so compelling persons for the\npurposes of this Division."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-30-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-30"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-30-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
