      },
      "cml:operator": "must",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Expresses a requirement",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-32",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "32 Tribunal immunity certificates",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-32"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.36",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An authenticated Tribunal immunity certificate is admissible in\nproceedings under this Division as prima facie evidence of matters\nstated in the certificate.\n(2) In this section:\nTribunal immunity certificate means a certificate or declaration\nthat:\n(a) is given or made by a Tribunal under the Statute of the\nTribunal or under the rules adopted under the Statute of the\nTribunal; and\n(b) specifies or declares that, under the Statute of the Tribunal or\nunder the rules adopted under the Statute of the Tribunal,\npersons generally or a specified person could or could not:\n(i) either generally or in specified proceedings; and\n(ii) either generally or in specified circumstances;\nbe required to answer a specified question or to produce a specified\ndocument.\n\n\nOther forms of assistance to a Tribunal  Part 4\nRequests for surveillance devices  Division 1A\nSection 32A\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nCompilation date: 28/03/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An authenticated Tribunal immunity certificate is admissible in\nproceedings under this Division as prima facie evidence of matters\nstated in the certificate.\n(2) In this section:\nTribunal immunity certificate means a certificate or declaration\nthat:\n(a) is given or made by a Tribunal under the Statute of the\nTribunal or under the rules adopted under the Statute of the\nTribunal; and\n(b) specifies or declares that, under the Statute of the Tribunal or\nunder the rules adopted under the Statute of the Tribunal,\npersons generally or a specified person could or could not:\n(i) either generally or in specified proceedings; and\n(ii) either generally or in specified circumstances;\nbe required to answer a specified question or to produce a specified\ndocument.\n\n\nOther forms of assistance to a Tribunal  Part 4\nRequests for surveillance devices  Division 1A\nSection 32A\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nCompilation date: 28/03/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-32-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-32-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "c4bd4262c042a005135e53be530cc1433c16f8bb6992f7080d63d2263796af0f"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-32",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "32 Tribunal immunity certificates",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 36,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An authenticated Tribunal immunity certificate is admissible in\nproceedings under this Division as prima facie evidence of matters\nstated in the certificate.\n(2) In this section:\nTribunal immunity certificate means a certificate or declaration\nthat:\n(a) is given or made by a Tribunal under the Statute of the\nTribunal or under the rules adopted under the Statute of the\nTribunal; and\n(b) specifies or declares that, under the Statute of the Tribunal or\nunder the rules adopted under the Statute of the Tribunal,\npersons generally or a specified person could or could not:\n(i) either generally or in specified proceedings; and\n(ii) either generally or in specified circumstances;\nbe required to answer a specified question or to produce a specified\ndocument.\n\n\nOther forms of assistance to a Tribunal  Part 4\nRequests for surveillance devices  Division 1A\nSection 32A\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nCompilation date: 28/03/2026"
    },
    {
