      "cof:title": "32C Providing forensic evidence to the Tribunal",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 41,
      "values:originalText": "(1) The Attorney-General may direct a constable about how forensic\nevidence is to be provided to a Tribunal if:\n(a) the Attorney-General gave an authorisation to the constable\nunder subsection 32B(1); and\n(b) the forensic evidence resulted from the authorisation.\n(2) A direction under subsection (1) is not a legislative instrument."
    },
