      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "authorise",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Granting authority",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "The Attorney-General may authorise...",
      "cml:conclusionText": "...the Australian Federal Police or the police force..."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-34b",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "34B Authorising an authorisation for the disclosure of prospective",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-34b"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.45",
      "values:originalText": "telecommunications data\n(1) The Attorney-General may authorise, in writing, the making of an\nauthorisation under section 180B of the Telecommunications\n(Interception and Access) Act 1979 for the disclosure of\ninformation or documents if:\n(a) a Tribunal has requested the Attorney-General to arrange for\nthe disclosure of the information or documents; and\n(b) the information or documents come into existence during a\nperiod specified by the Tribunal, and which started on or\nafter the day the request was made; and\n(c) the Attorney-General is satisfied that:\n(i) a proceeding is before, or an investigation is being\nconducted by, the Tribunal; and\n(ii) the information or documents relate to the fact of a\ncommunication passing over a telecommunications\nsystem during a period specified in the Tribunal’s\nrequest.\nNote:\nThe information or documents will not be disclosed unless they are\nreasonably necessary for the investigation or proceeding (see\nsubsection 180B(3) of that Act).\n(2) To avoid doubt, information or documents do not relate to the fact\nof a communication passing over a telecommunications system to\nthe extent that the information is, or the documents contain, the\ncontents or substance of a communication.",
      "skos:definition": "telecommunications data\n(1) The Attorney-General may authorise, in writing, the making of an\nauthorisation under section 180B of the Telecommunications\n(Interception and Access) Act 1979 for the disclosure of\ninformation or documents if:\n(a) a Tribunal has requested the Attorney-General to arrange for\nthe disclosure of the information or documents; and\n(b) the information or documents come into existence during a\nperiod specified by the Tribunal, and which started on or\nafter the day the request was made; and\n(c) the Attorney-General is satisfied that:\n(i) a proceeding is before, or an investigation is being\nconducted by, the Tribunal; and\n(ii) the information or documents relate to the fact of a\ncommunication passing over a telecommunications\nsystem during a period specified in the Tribunal’s\nrequest.\nNote:\nThe information or documents will not be disclosed unless they are\nreasonably necessary for the investigation or proceeding (see\nsubsection 180B(3) of that Act).\n(2) To avoid doubt, information or documents do not relate to the fact\nof a communication passing over a telecommunications system to\nthe extent that the information is, or the documents contain, the\ncontents or substance of a communication.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-34b-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-34b-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "572b36c74482d8a36327f6d3989c6649f68f32687bb793f5a0c22e4b94497e5d"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-34b",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "34B Authorising an authorisation for the disclosure of prospective",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 45,
      "values:originalText": "telecommunications data\n(1) The Attorney-General may authorise, in writing, the making of an\nauthorisation under section 180B of the Telecommunications\n(Interception and Access) Act 1979 for the disclosure of\ninformation or documents if:\n(a) a Tribunal has requested the Attorney-General to arrange for\nthe disclosure of the information or documents; and\n(b) the information or documents come into existence during a\nperiod specified by the Tribunal, and which started on or\nafter the day the request was made; and\n(c) the Attorney-General is satisfied that:\n(i) a proceeding is before, or an investigation is being\nconducted by, the Tribunal; and\n(ii) the information or documents relate to the fact of a\ncommunication passing over a telecommunications\nsystem during a period specified in the Tribunal’s\nrequest.\nNote:\nThe information or documents will not be disclosed unless they are\nreasonably necessary for the investigation or proceeding (see\nsubsection 180B(3) of that Act).\n(2) To avoid doubt, information or documents do not relate to the fact\nof a communication passing over a telecommunications system to\nthe extent that the information is, or the documents contain, the\ncontents or substance of a communication."
    },
