        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-35-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "51bb0f4cd5ad26528fa433e5d148fae3cec08d2d7eb5916e8a53a5e3844da1de",
      "skos:note": "Attorney-General must not comply with request if it would prejudice Australia's sovereignty, security or national interest."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-35-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "35(2) Persons giving evidence or assisting (other than prisoners)",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 46,
      "values:originalText": "(2) The Attorney-General must not comply with the request if, in his\nor her opinion:\n(a) complying with the request would prejudice Australia’s\nsovereignty, security or national interest; or\n(b) there are special circumstances justifying non-compliance.\n\n\nOther forms of assistance to a Tribunal  Part 4\nGiving evidence at hearings, or assisting in investigations, in foreign countries  Division\nSection 36\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nCompilation date: 28/03/2026"
    },
    {
