      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.47",
      "values:originalText": "(2) Subject to subsection (4), if the prisoner is being held in custody,\nthe Attorney-General may:\n(a) if the prisoner is a federal prisoner and is not also a State\nprisoner-direct that the prisoner be released from prison for\nthe purpose of travelling to the foreign country to give\nevidence at the proceeding or to assist the investigation; and\n(b) if the prisoner is a federal prisoner and also a State\nprisoner-direct, subject to the obtaining of any approvals\nrequired to be obtained from an authority of the relevant\nState, that the prisoner be released from prison for the\npurpose of such travel; and\n(c) in any case-subject to the making or giving of any necessary\ndirections or approvals relevant to release of the prisoner,\nmake arrangements for such travel in the custody of a police",
      "skos:definition": "(2) Subject to subsection (4), if the prisoner is being held in custody,\nthe Attorney-General may:\n(a) if the prisoner is a federal prisoner and is not also a State\nprisoner-direct that the prisoner be released from prison for\nthe purpose of travelling to the foreign country to give\nevidence at the proceeding or to assist the investigation; and\n(b) if the prisoner is a federal prisoner and also a State\nprisoner-direct, subject to the obtaining of any approvals\nrequired to be obtained from an authority of the relevant\nState, that the prisoner be released from prison for the\npurpose of such travel; and\n(c) in any case-subject to the making or giving of any necessary\ndirections or approvals relevant to release of the prisoner,\nmake arrangements for such travel in the custody of a police",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-36"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-36-ss-2-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-36-ss-2-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-36-ss-2-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-36-ss-2-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-36-ss-2-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-36-ss-2-logic-argumentation-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "dfcf460ee3fef9ce072a938f070fff402f4f78fe60572fafb4ad54b189dd6c4e",
      "skos:note": "Release of prisoner for travel to give evidence or assist investigation."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-36-ss-2",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "36(2) Prisoners giving evidence or assisting",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 47,
      "values:originalText": "(2) Subject to subsection (4), if the prisoner is being held in custody,\nthe Attorney-General may:\n(a) if the prisoner is a federal prisoner and is not also a State\nprisoner-direct that the prisoner be released from prison for\nthe purpose of travelling to the foreign country to give\nevidence at the proceeding or to assist the investigation; and\n(b) if the prisoner is a federal prisoner and also a State\nprisoner-direct, subject to the obtaining of any approvals\nrequired to be obtained from an authority of the relevant\nState, that the prisoner be released from prison for the\npurpose of such travel; and\n(c) in any case-subject to the making or giving of any necessary\ndirections or approvals relevant to release of the prisoner,\nmake arrangements for such travel in the custody of a police"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-36-ss-2-norm",
