      "skos:note": "Transportation of a person in custody not continued within a reasonable time."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-39-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "39(3) Transit",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 50,
      "values:originalText": "(3) If:\n(a) a person is being held in custody pursuant to a direction\nunder subsection (2); and\n(b) the person’s transportation is not, in the Attorney-General’s\nopinion, continued within a reasonable time;\nthe Attorney-General may direct that the person be transported in\ncustody to the foreign country from which the person was first\ntransported.\n\n\nOther forms of assistance to a Tribunal  Part 4\nService of process  Division 5\nSection 40\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nCompilation date: 28/03/2026"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-39-ss-3-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-39-ss-3"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-39-ss-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "Prohibit",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Prohibition of transportation",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 0.5,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "(a) a person is being held in custody pursuant to a direction under subsection (2); and (b) the person’s transportation is not, in the Attorney-General’s opinion, continued within a reasonable time;",
      "cml:conclusionText": "the Attorney-General may direct that the person be transported in custody to the foreign country from which the person was first transported."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-40",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40 Service of process",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-40"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.51",
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), if a Tribunal requests the\nAttorney-General to arrange for service in Australia of a process\nrelating to a proceeding before, or an investigation conducted by,\nthe Tribunal, the Attorney-General may arrange for service of the\nprocess.\n(2) The Attorney-General must not comply with the request if, in his\nor her opinion:\n(a) complying with the request would prejudice Australia’s\nsovereignty, security or national interest; or\n(b) there are special circumstances justifying non-compliance.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), if a Tribunal requests the\nAttorney-General to arrange for service in Australia of a process\nrelating to a proceeding before, or an investigation conducted by,\nthe Tribunal, the Attorney-General may arrange for service of the\nprocess.\n(2) The Attorney-General must not comply with the request if, in his\nor her opinion:\n(a) complying with the request would prejudice Australia’s\nsovereignty, security or national interest; or\n(b) there are special circumstances justifying non-compliance.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-40-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-40-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "3b599a501f5f7938d57fff29a580e3a410eda861341459a34cb7aec9af7c1e87"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-40",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40 Service of process",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 51,
      "values:originalText": "(1) Subject to subsection (2), if a Tribunal requests the\nAttorney-General to arrange for service in Australia of a process\nrelating to a proceeding before, or an investigation conducted by,\nthe Tribunal, the Attorney-General may arrange for service of the\nprocess.\n(2) The Attorney-General must not comply with the request if, in his\nor her opinion:\n(a) complying with the request would prejudice Australia’s\nsovereignty, security or national interest; or\n(b) there are special circumstances justifying non-compliance."
    },
