    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-40ao",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40AO Passing on information given under monitoring orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-40ao"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.60",
      "values:originalText": "If an enforcement agency is given information under a monitoring\norder made in relation to the Tribunal offence, the enforcement\nagency must, as soon as practicable after receiving the information,\npass the information on to:\n(a) the Attorney-General; or\n(b) an APS employee who is in the Department and who is\nspecified by the Attorney-General by written notice to the\nenforcement agency.\nSubdivision F—Search warrants relating to proceeds of crime\nand evidential material",
      "skos:definition": "If an enforcement agency is given information under a monitoring\norder made in relation to the Tribunal offence, the enforcement\nagency must, as soon as practicable after receiving the information,\npass the information on to:\n(a) the Attorney-General; or\n(b) an APS employee who is in the Department and who is\nspecified by the Attorney-General by written notice to the\nenforcement agency.\nSubdivision F—Search warrants relating to proceeds of crime\nand evidential material",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-40ao-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-40ao-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "331f7a50d6e047409346c438c56590bcb5b3fb20e89d2960d51d69bbf32df4b2",
      "skos:note": "Must pass information on to Attorney-General or APS employee",
      "dc:description": "Information under monitoring order"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-40ao",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40AO Passing on information given under monitoring orders",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 60,
      "values:originalText": "If an enforcement agency is given information under a monitoring\norder made in relation to the Tribunal offence, the enforcement\nagency must, as soon as practicable after receiving the information,\npass the information on to:\n(a) the Attorney-General; or\n(b) an APS employee who is in the Department and who is\nspecified by the Attorney-General by written notice to the\nenforcement agency.\nSubdivision F—Search warrants relating to proceeds of crime\nand evidential material"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-40ao-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-40ao"
      },
      "values:deonticStatus": {
        "@id": "values:HeuristicDerived"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "values:borneBy": {
        "@id": "values:Agent"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-40ao-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "MUST",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Obligation to pass information on",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      }
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-40ap",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40AP Applying for and issuing search warrants",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-40ap"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.60",
      "values:originalText": "(1) An authorised officer may apply for a search warrant under the\nProceeds of Crime Act 2002 in respect of the Tribunal offence that\nis the subject of the proceeds request, if authorised to do so by the\nAttorney-General under section 40AB.\n(2) Part 3-5 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 applies to the\napplication, and to any POCA search warrant issued as a result.\n(3) That Part applies as if:\n(a) a reference in that Part to tainted property were a reference to\nproceeds of the Tribunal offence that is the subject of the\nproceeds request; and\n(b) a reference in that Part to evidential material were a reference\nto evidential material as defined in section 4 of this Act for\nthe purposes of this Subdivision; and\n(c) the words “or section 40AS, 40AT or 40AU of the\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995” were inserted\nafter “this Act” in paragraph 254(1)(a) of the Proceeds of\nCrime Act 2002; and\n\n\nOther forms of assistance to a Tribunal  Part 4\nIdentification, tracing, and freezing or seizure, of proceeds of Tribunal offences",
      "skos:definition": "(1) An authorised officer may apply for a search warrant under the\nProceeds of Crime Act 2002 in respect of the Tribunal offence that\nis the subject of the proceeds request, if authorised to do so by the\nAttorney-General under section 40AB.\n(2) Part 3-5 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 applies to the\napplication, and to any POCA search warrant issued as a result.\n(3) That Part applies as if:\n(a) a reference in that Part to tainted property were a reference to\nproceeds of the Tribunal offence that is the subject of the\nproceeds request; and\n(b) a reference in that Part to evidential material were a reference\nto evidential material as defined in section 4 of this Act for\nthe purposes of this Subdivision; and\n(c) the words “or section 40AS, 40AT or 40AU of the\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995” were inserted\nafter “this Act” in paragraph 254(1)(a) of the Proceeds of\nCrime Act 2002; and\n\n\nOther forms of assistance to a Tribunal  Part 4\nIdentification, tracing, and freezing or seizure, of proceeds of Tribunal offences",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-40ap-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-40ap-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-40ap-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "d22ecb11377d1807abbaaa35af3b959cc16007b03450c521d19f616f0f8271e5"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-40ap",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40AP Applying for and issuing search warrants",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 60,
      "values:originalText": "(1) An authorised officer may apply for a search warrant under the\nProceeds of Crime Act 2002 in respect of the Tribunal offence that\nis the subject of the proceeds request, if authorised to do so by the\nAttorney-General under section 40AB.\n(2) Part 3-5 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 applies to the\napplication, and to any POCA search warrant issued as a result.\n(3) That Part applies as if:\n(a) a reference in that Part to tainted property were a reference to\nproceeds of the Tribunal offence that is the subject of the\nproceeds request; and\n(b) a reference in that Part to evidential material were a reference\nto evidential material as defined in section 4 of this Act for\nthe purposes of this Subdivision; and\n(c) the words “or section 40AS, 40AT or 40AU of the\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995” were inserted\nafter “this Act” in paragraph 254(1)(a) of the Proceeds of\nCrime Act 2002; and\n\n\nOther forms of assistance to a Tribunal  Part 4\nIdentification, tracing, and freezing or seizure, of proceeds of Tribunal offences"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-40ap-ss-1",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40AP(1) Applying for and issuing search warrants",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-40ap-ss-1"
      },
