      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.62",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person who claims an interest in property that has been seized\nunder a POCA search warrant in relation to a Tribunal offence may\napply to a court for an order that the property be returned to the\nperson.\n(2) The court must be a court of the State or Territory in which the\nPOCA search warrant was issued that has proceeds jurisdiction.\n\n\nOther forms of assistance to a Tribunal  Part 4\nIdentification, tracing, and freezing or seizure, of proceeds of Tribunal offences",
