    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-40au",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "40AU Dealing with evidential material and certain property or",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-40au"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.65",
      "values:originalText": "things seized under POCA search warrants\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) property or a thing (the seized item) is seized under a POCA\nsearch warrant in relation to a Tribunal offence; and\n(b) the seized item is:\n(i) evidential material; or\n(ii) property or a thing of a kind referred to in\nsubparagraph 40AR(a)(iv); and\n(c) the seized item is seized by a person (the seizing officer) who\nis:\n(i) an authorised officer; or\n(ii) a person assisting in relation to the warrant.\n(2) The seizing officer may retain the seized item for a period not\nexceeding 1 month pending a written direction from the\nAttorney-General as to how to deal with the seized item.\n(3) Without limiting the directions that may be given under\nsubsection (2), the Attorney-General may direct the seizing officer\nto send the seized item to the Tribunal.",
      "skos:definition": "things seized under POCA search warrants\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) property or a thing (the seized item) is seized under a POCA\nsearch warrant in relation to a Tribunal offence; and\n(b) the seized item is:\n(i) evidential material; or\n(ii) property or a thing of a kind referred to in\nsubparagraph 40AR(a)(iv); and\n(c) the seized item is seized by a person (the seizing officer) who\nis:\n(i) an authorised officer; or\n(ii) a person assisting in relation to the warrant.\n(2) The seizing officer may retain the seized item for a period not\nexceeding 1 month pending a written direction from the\nAttorney-General as to how to deal with the seized item.\n(3) Without limiting the directions that may be given under\nsubsection (2), the Attorney-General may direct the seizing officer\nto send the seized item to the Tribunal.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-40au-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-40au-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-40au-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "61e9bb2be232e039264e3061e24b8e6634f4bfb7f851d87062ac54abf3eba7f4"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-40au",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "40AU Dealing with evidential material and certain property or",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 65,
      "values:originalText": "things seized under POCA search warrants\n(1) This section applies if:\n(a) property or a thing (the seized item) is seized under a POCA\nsearch warrant in relation to a Tribunal offence; and\n(b) the seized item is:\n(i) evidential material; or\n(ii) property or a thing of a kind referred to in\nsubparagraph 40AR(a)(iv); and\n(c) the seized item is seized by a person (the seizing officer) who\nis:\n(i) an authorised officer; or\n(ii) a person assisting in relation to the warrant.\n(2) The seizing officer may retain the seized item for a period not\nexceeding 1 month pending a written direction from the\nAttorney-General as to how to deal with the seized item.\n(3) Without limiting the directions that may be given under\nsubsection (2), the Attorney-General may direct the seizing officer\nto send the seized item to the Tribunal."
    },
