    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-45",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "45 Registration of order",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-45"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.68",
      "values:originalText": "(1AA) An application for the registration of an order in accordance with\nan authorisation under subsection 44(1) must be to a court with\nproceeds jurisdiction.\n(1) If a proceeds of crime authority so applies to a court with proceeds\njurisdiction, the court must register the order, unless the court is\nsatisfied that it would be contrary to the interests of justice to do\nso.\n(1A) The proceeds of crime authority must give notice of the\napplication:\n\n\nForfeiture of proceeds of Tribunal offences  Part 6\n\nSection 46\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nCompilation date: 28/03/2026\n(a) to specified persons the authority has reason to suspect may\nhave an interest in the property; and\n(b) to such other persons as the court directs.\n(1B) However, the court may consider the application without notice\nhaving been given if the proceeds of crime authority requests the\ncourt to do so.\n(2) An order must be registered in a court by the registration, under the\nrules of the court, of a copy of the appropriate order sealed by the\nTribunal.\n(3) Subject to subsection 46(2), if a copy of a sealed copy of an order\nis faxed, emailed or sent by other electronic means, it is taken for\nthe purposes of subsection (2) of this section to be the same as the\nsealed copy.",
      "skos:definition": "(1AA) An application for the registration of an order in accordance with\nan authorisation under subsection 44(1) must be to a court with\nproceeds jurisdiction.\n(1) If a proceeds of crime authority so applies to a court with proceeds\njurisdiction, the court must register the order, unless the court is\nsatisfied that it would be contrary to the interests of justice to do\nso.\n(1A) The proceeds of crime authority must give notice of the\napplication:\n\n\nForfeiture of proceeds of Tribunal offences  Part 6\n\nSection 46\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nCompilation date: 28/03/2026\n(a) to specified persons the authority has reason to suspect may\nhave an interest in the property; and\n(b) to such other persons as the court directs.\n(1B) However, the court may consider the application without notice\nhaving been given if the proceeds of crime authority requests the\ncourt to do so.\n(2) An order must be registered in a court by the registration, under the\nrules of the court, of a copy of the appropriate order sealed by the\nTribunal.\n(3) Subject to subsection 46(2), if a copy of a sealed copy of an order\nis faxed, emailed or sent by other electronic means, it is taken for\nthe purposes of subsection (2) of this section to be the same as the\nsealed copy.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-45-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-45-ss-1a"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-45-ss-1b"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-45-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-45-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "2ad169045c43501e299d0a73cb587b88f05f6f1ce6e028fb5b12d6ca5464c5b9"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-45",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "45 Registration of order",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 68,
      "values:originalText": "(1AA) An application for the registration of an order in accordance with\nan authorisation under subsection 44(1) must be to a court with\nproceeds jurisdiction.\n(1) If a proceeds of crime authority so applies to a court with proceeds\njurisdiction, the court must register the order, unless the court is\nsatisfied that it would be contrary to the interests of justice to do\nso.\n(1A) The proceeds of crime authority must give notice of the\napplication:\n\n\nForfeiture of proceeds of Tribunal offences  Part 6\n\nSection 46\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nCompilation date: 28/03/2026\n(a) to specified persons the authority has reason to suspect may\nhave an interest in the property; and\n(b) to such other persons as the court directs.\n(1B) However, the court may consider the application without notice\nhaving been given if the proceeds of crime authority requests the\ncourt to do so.\n(2) An order must be registered in a court by the registration, under the\nrules of the court, of a copy of the appropriate order sealed by the\nTribunal.\n(3) Subject to subsection 46(2), if a copy of a sealed copy of an order\nis faxed, emailed or sent by other electronic means, it is taken for\nthe purposes of subsection (2) of this section to be the same as the\nsealed copy."
    },
