    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-46",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "46 Effect of order",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-46"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.69",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A forfeiture order registered in a court has effect, and may be\nenforced, as if it were a forfeiture order made by the court under\nthe Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 at the time of registration.\n(1A) In particular, section 68 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 applies\nin relation to the forfeiture order as if:\n(a) the reference in subparagraph 68(1)(b)(i) of that Act to a\nproceeds of crime authority having applied for the order were\na reference to the authority having applied for registration of\nthe order under section 45 of this Act; and\n(b) subparagraph 68(1)(b)(ii) of that Act were repealed.\n(2) A registration effected by a court registering a copy of a sealed\ncopy ceases to have effect after 45 days unless the sealed copy has\nbeen filed by then in that court.\n(3) Subject to section 46A, property that is subject to an order\nregistered under this Part may be disposed of, or otherwise dealt\nwith, in accordance with any direction of the Attorney-General or",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A forfeiture order registered in a court has effect, and may be\nenforced, as if it were a forfeiture order made by the court under\nthe Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 at the time of registration.\n(1A) In particular, section 68 of the Proceeds of Crime Act 2002 applies\nin relation to the forfeiture order as if:\n(a) the reference in subparagraph 68(1)(b)(i) of that Act to a\nproceeds of crime authority having applied for the order were\na reference to the authority having applied for registration of\nthe order under section 45 of this Act; and\n(b) subparagraph 68(1)(b)(ii) of that Act were repealed.\n(2) A registration effected by a court registering a copy of a sealed\ncopy ceases to have effect after 45 days unless the sealed copy has\nbeen filed by then in that court.\n(3) Subject to section 46A, property that is subject to an order\nregistered under this Part may be disposed of, or otherwise dealt\nwith, in accordance with any direction of the Attorney-General or",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-46-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-46-ss-1a"
        },
