      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.70",
      "values:originalText": "(1) If a court registers under section 45 a forfeiture order against\nproperty, a person who:\n(a) claims an interest in the property; and\n(b) was not convicted of an offence in respect of which the order\nwas made;\nmay apply to the court for an order under subsection (2).\nOrders by the court",
      "skos:definition": "(1) If a court registers under section 45 a forfeiture order against\nproperty, a person who:\n(a) claims an interest in the property; and\n(b) was not convicted of an offence in respect of which the order\nwas made;\nmay apply to the court for an order under subsection (2).\nOrders by the court",
