    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-46a-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "46A(5) Effect on third parties of registration of forfeiture orders",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-46a-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.70",
      "values:originalText": "(5) Without limiting subsection (4), the court may grant a person leave\nif the court is satisfied that:\n(a) the person, for a good reason, did not attend the hearing\nreferred to in subsection (3) although the person had notice of\nthe hearing; or\n(b) particular evidence that the person proposes to adduce in\nconnection with the proposed application under\nsubsection (1) was not available to the person at the time of\nthe hearing referred to in subsection (3).\nPeriod for applying",
      "skos:definition": "(5) Without limiting subsection (4), the court may grant a person leave\nif the court is satisfied that:\n(a) the person, for a good reason, did not attend the hearing\nreferred to in subsection (3) although the person had notice of\nthe hearing; or\n(b) particular evidence that the person proposes to adduce in\nconnection with the proposed application under\nsubsection (1) was not available to the person at the time of\nthe hearing referred to in subsection (3).\nPeriod for applying",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-46a"
