    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-48-ss-3",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "48(3) Content of warrants",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-48-ss-3"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.74",
      "values:originalText": "(3) The magistrate is also to state, in a warrant in relation to premises:\n(a) that the warrant authorises the seizure of a thing (other than\nevidential material of the kind referred to in paragraph (1)(c))\nfound at the premises in the course of the search that the\nexecuting officer or an officer assisting believes on\nreasonable grounds to be:\n(i) evidential material; or\n(ii) a thing relevant to an indictable offence against an\nAustralian law;\nif the executing officer or an officer assisting believes on\nreasonable grounds that seizure of the thing is necessary to\nprevent its concealment, loss or destruction or its use in\ncommitting a Tribunal offence or an indictable offence\nagainst an Australian law; and\n(b) whether the warrant authorises an ordinary search or a frisk\nsearch of a person who is at or near the premises when the\nwarrant is executed if the executing officer or an officer\nassisting suspects on reasonable grounds that the person has\nany evidential material or seizable items in his or her\npossession.",
      "skos:definition": "(3) The magistrate is also to state, in a warrant in relation to premises:\n(a) that the warrant authorises the seizure of a thing (other than\nevidential material of the kind referred to in paragraph (1)(c))\nfound at the premises in the course of the search that the\nexecuting officer or an officer assisting believes on\nreasonable grounds to be:\n(i) evidential material; or\n(ii) a thing relevant to an indictable offence against an\nAustralian law;\nif the executing officer or an officer assisting believes on\nreasonable grounds that seizure of the thing is necessary to\nprevent its concealment, loss or destruction or its use in\ncommitting a Tribunal offence or an indictable offence\nagainst an Australian law; and\n(b) whether the warrant authorises an ordinary search or a frisk\nsearch of a person who is at or near the premises when the\nwarrant is executed if the executing officer or an officer\nassisting suspects on reasonable grounds that the person has\nany evidential material or seizable items in his or her\npossession.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-48"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-48-ss-3-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-48-ss-3-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "4c8218ef31dc48b27bdb8285322b29796726d5ec2911deba4a69733a5e0ab689",
      "skos:note": "Seizure of evidential material or seizable items without warrant is prohibited."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-48-ss-3",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "48(3) Content of warrants",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 74,
      "values:originalText": "(3) The magistrate is also to state, in a warrant in relation to premises:\n(a) that the warrant authorises the seizure of a thing (other than\nevidential material of the kind referred to in paragraph (1)(c))\nfound at the premises in the course of the search that the\nexecuting officer or an officer assisting believes on\nreasonable grounds to be:\n(i) evidential material; or\n(ii) a thing relevant to an indictable offence against an\nAustralian law;\nif the executing officer or an officer assisting believes on\nreasonable grounds that seizure of the thing is necessary to\nprevent its concealment, loss or destruction or its use in\ncommitting a Tribunal offence or an indictable offence\nagainst an Australian law; and\n(b) whether the warrant authorises an ordinary search or a frisk\nsearch of a person who is at or near the premises when the\nwarrant is executed if the executing officer or an officer\nassisting suspects on reasonable grounds that the person has\nany evidential material or seizable items in his or her\npossession."
    },
