      "cml:conclusionText": "The artificial agent asserts that the execution is restricted to the specified hours."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-50",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "50 The things authorised by a search warrant in relation to a person",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-50"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.77",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A warrant in force in relation to a person authorises the executing\nofficer or an officer assisting:\n(a) to:\n(i) search the person as specified in the warrant; and\n(ii) search things found in the possession of the person; and\n(iii) search any recently used conveyance;\nfor things of the kind specified in the warrant; and\n(b) to:\n(i) seize things of that kind; and\n(ii) record fingerprints from things; and\n(iii) take forensic samples from things;\nfound in the course of the search; and\n(c) to seize other things found in the possession of the person or\nin or on the conveyance in the course of the search that the\nexecuting officer or an officer assisting believes on\nreasonable grounds to be:\n(i) evidential material; or\n(ii) things relevant to an indictable offence against an\nAustralian law;\nif the executing officer or a police officer assisting believes\non reasonable grounds that seizure of the things is necessary\nto prevent their concealment, loss or destruction or their use",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A warrant in force in relation to a person authorises the executing\nofficer or an officer assisting:\n(a) to:\n(i) search the person as specified in the warrant; and\n(ii) search things found in the possession of the person; and\n(iii) search any recently used conveyance;\nfor things of the kind specified in the warrant; and\n(b) to:\n(i) seize things of that kind; and\n(ii) record fingerprints from things; and\n(iii) take forensic samples from things;\nfound in the course of the search; and\n(c) to seize other things found in the possession of the person or\nin or on the conveyance in the course of the search that the\nexecuting officer or an officer assisting believes on\nreasonable grounds to be:\n(i) evidential material; or\n(ii) things relevant to an indictable offence against an\nAustralian law;\nif the executing officer or a police officer assisting believes\non reasonable grounds that seizure of the things is necessary\nto prevent their concealment, loss or destruction or their use",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-50-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-50-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "226669d42b8cf81c71ba206f8a0f82a690dd1fe6f5db945821c58d90bace393b",
      "skos:note": "Seizure of things is prohibited unless on reasonable grounds believed necessary to prevent concealment, loss or destruction."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-50",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "50 The things authorised by a search warrant in relation to a person",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 77,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A warrant in force in relation to a person authorises the executing\nofficer or an officer assisting:\n(a) to:\n(i) search the person as specified in the warrant; and\n(ii) search things found in the possession of the person; and\n(iii) search any recently used conveyance;\nfor things of the kind specified in the warrant; and\n(b) to:\n(i) seize things of that kind; and\n(ii) record fingerprints from things; and\n(iii) take forensic samples from things;\nfound in the course of the search; and\n(c) to seize other things found in the possession of the person or\nin or on the conveyance in the course of the search that the\nexecuting officer or an officer assisting believes on\nreasonable grounds to be:\n(i) evidential material; or\n(ii) things relevant to an indictable offence against an\nAustralian law;\nif the executing officer or a police officer assisting believes\non reasonable grounds that seizure of the things is necessary\nto prevent their concealment, loss or destruction or their use"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-50-norm",
      "@type": "values:Prohibition",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-50"
