    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-51-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "51(4) Restrictions on personal searches",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-51-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.78",
      "values:originalText": "(4) If an application is made to a magistrate under this section and the\nmagistrate, after considering the information and having received\nand considered such further information (if any) as the magistrate\nrequires, is satisfied that:\n\n\nSearch, seizure and powers of arrest  Part 7\nSearch warrants  Division 1\nSection 53\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nCompilation date: 28/03/2026\n(a) a warrant in the terms of the application should be issued\nurgently; or\n(b) the delay that would occur if an application were made in\nperson would frustrate the effective execution of the warrant;\nthe magistrate may complete and sign the same form of warrant\nthat would be issued under section 47.\n53  Formalities relating to warrants issued by telephone etc.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) If an application is made to a magistrate under this section and the\nmagistrate, after considering the information and having received\nand considered such further information (if any) as the magistrate\nrequires, is satisfied that:\n\n\nSearch, seizure and powers of arrest  Part 7\nSearch warrants  Division 1\nSection 53\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nCompilation date: 28/03/2026\n(a) a warrant in the terms of the application should be issued\nurgently; or\n(b) the delay that would occur if an application were made in\nperson would frustrate the effective execution of the warrant;\nthe magistrate may complete and sign the same form of warrant\nthat would be issued under section 47.\n53  Formalities relating to warrants issued by telephone etc.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-51"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-51-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-51-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-51-ss-4-logic-deontic-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "f04a701fbfbc3fd2649b285abec93d51981673642ca3b12c68643d37e277c75d",
      "skos:note": "Magistrate must complete warrant form for documents Magistrate may issue warrant urgently or complete and sign form of warrant",
      "dc:description": "warrant form"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-51-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "51(4) Restrictions on personal searches",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 78,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If an application is made to a magistrate under this section and the\nmagistrate, after considering the information and having received\nand considered such further information (if any) as the magistrate\nrequires, is satisfied that:\n\n\nSearch, seizure and powers of arrest  Part 7\nSearch warrants  Division 1\nSection 53\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nCompilation date: 28/03/2026\n(a) a warrant in the terms of the application should be issued\nurgently; or\n(b) the delay that would occur if an application were made in\nperson would frustrate the effective execution of the warrant;\nthe magistrate may complete and sign the same form of warrant\nthat would be issued under section 47.\n53  Formalities relating to warrants issued by telephone etc."
    },
