      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 82,
      "values:originalText": "(2) If the executing officer or an officer assisting, after operating the\nequipment, finds that evidential material is accessible by doing so,\nhe or she may:\n(a) seize the equipment and any disk, tape or other associated\ndevice; or\n\n\nSearch, seizure and powers of arrest  Part 7\nProvisions relating to execution of search warrants  Division 2\nSection 58\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nCompilation date: 28/03/2026\n(b) if the material can, by using facilities at the premises, be put\nin a documentary form-operate the facilities to put the\nmaterial in that form and seize the documents so produced; or\n(c) if the material can be transferred to a disk, tape or other\nstorage device:\n(i) that is brought to the premises; or\n(ii) that is at the premises and the use of which for the\npurpose has been agreed to in writing by the occupier of\nthe premises;\noperate the equipment or other facilities to copy the material\nto the storage device and take the storage device from the\npremises."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-58-ss-2-norm",
