    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-58-ss-4",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "58(4) Use of electronic equipment at premises",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-58-ss-4"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.82",
      "values:originalText": "(4) If the executing officer or an officer assisting believes on\nreasonable grounds that:\n(a) evidential material may be accessible by operating electronic\nequipment at the warrant premises; and\n(b) expert assistance is required to operate the equipment; and\n(c) if he or she does not take action under this subsection, the\nmaterial may be destroyed, altered or otherwise interfered\nwith;\nhe or she may do whatever is necessary to secure the equipment,\nwhether by locking it up, placing a guard or otherwise.",
      "skos:definition": "(4) If the executing officer or an officer assisting believes on\nreasonable grounds that:\n(a) evidential material may be accessible by operating electronic\nequipment at the warrant premises; and\n(b) expert assistance is required to operate the equipment; and\n(c) if he or she does not take action under this subsection, the\nmaterial may be destroyed, altered or otherwise interfered\nwith;\nhe or she may do whatever is necessary to secure the equipment,\nwhether by locking it up, placing a guard or otherwise.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-58"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-58-ss-4-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-58-ss-4-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-58-ss-4-logic-deontic-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-58-ss-4-logic-deontic-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-58-ss-4-logic-alleninterval-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-58-ss-4-logic-ltl-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "48ac4065c7ef8771244c046ccb40502637126724ba653d938534f64ee3742207",
      "skos:note": "Executing officer may take necessary actions to secure electronic equipment at premises."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-58-ss-4",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "58(4) Use of electronic equipment at premises",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 82,
      "values:originalText": "(4) If the executing officer or an officer assisting believes on\nreasonable grounds that:\n(a) evidential material may be accessible by operating electronic\nequipment at the warrant premises; and\n(b) expert assistance is required to operate the equipment; and\n(c) if he or she does not take action under this subsection, the\nmaterial may be destroyed, altered or otherwise interfered\nwith;\nhe or she may do whatever is necessary to secure the equipment,\nwhether by locking it up, placing a guard or otherwise."
    },
