      "cml:integrityHash": "6c29180725ab13bf7d4e18d3caa87562e9cfd9c455a4520a5e0363491fb64dad",
      "skos:note": "Police officer may conduct ordinary search of arrested person if suspecting they carry evidential material or seizable item."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-69",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "69 Power to conduct an ordinary search of an arrested person",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 91,
      "values:originalText": "A police officer who arrests a person under this Act or pursuant to\na warrant issued under this Act, or who is present at such an arrest,\nmay, if the police officer suspects on reasonable grounds that the\nperson is carrying:\n(a) evidential material relating to the Tribunal offence to which\nthe person’s custody relates; or\n(b) a seizable item;\nconduct an ordinary search of the person at or soon after the time\nof arrest, and seize any such thing found as a result of the search."
    },
