    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-72",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "72 Rules for conduct of strip search",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-72"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.93",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A strip search:\n(a) must be conducted in a private area; and\n(b) must be conducted by a police officer who is of the same sex\nas the person being searched; and\n(c) subject to subsections (3) and (4), must not be conducted in\nthe presence or view of a person who is of the opposite sex to\nthe person being searched; and\n(d) must not be conducted in the presence or view of a person\nwhose presence is not necessary for the purposes of the\nsearch; and\n(e) must not be conducted on a person who is under 10; and\n(f) if the person being searched is at least 10 but under 18, or is\nincapable of managing his or her affairs:\n(i) may only be conducted if a court orders that it be\nconducted; and\n(ii) must be conducted in the presence of a parent or\nguardian of the person being searched or, if that is not\nacceptable to the person, in the presence of another\nperson (other than a police officer) who is capable of\nrepresenting the interests of the person and who, as far\nas is practicable in the circumstances, is acceptable to\nthe person; and\n(g) must not involve a search of a person’s body cavities; and\n(h) must not involve the removal of more garments than the\npolice officer conducting the search believes on reasonable\ngrounds to be necessary to determine whether the person has\nin his or her possession the item searched for or to establish\nthe person’s involvement in the Tribunal offence to which\nthe person’s custody relates; and",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A strip search:\n(a) must be conducted in a private area; and\n(b) must be conducted by a police officer who is of the same sex\nas the person being searched; and\n(c) subject to subsections (3) and (4), must not be conducted in\nthe presence or view of a person who is of the opposite sex to\nthe person being searched; and\n(d) must not be conducted in the presence or view of a person\nwhose presence is not necessary for the purposes of the\nsearch; and\n(e) must not be conducted on a person who is under 10; and\n(f) if the person being searched is at least 10 but under 18, or is\nincapable of managing his or her affairs:\n(i) may only be conducted if a court orders that it be\nconducted; and\n(ii) must be conducted in the presence of a parent or\nguardian of the person being searched or, if that is not\nacceptable to the person, in the presence of another\nperson (other than a police officer) who is capable of\nrepresenting the interests of the person and who, as far\nas is practicable in the circumstances, is acceptable to\nthe person; and\n(g) must not involve a search of a person’s body cavities; and\n(h) must not involve the removal of more garments than the\npolice officer conducting the search believes on reasonable\ngrounds to be necessary to determine whether the person has\nin his or her possession the item searched for or to establish\nthe person’s involvement in the Tribunal offence to which\nthe person’s custody relates; and",
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-72-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-72-logic-deontic-1"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "6dc9d170e30bda086d1875976e33cdcaea1de33ba3051df83b56a9a949832570",
      "skos:note": "Strip search must be conducted under certain conditions."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-72",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "72 Rules for conduct of strip search",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 93,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A strip search:\n(a) must be conducted in a private area; and\n(b) must be conducted by a police officer who is of the same sex\nas the person being searched; and\n(c) subject to subsections (3) and (4), must not be conducted in\nthe presence or view of a person who is of the opposite sex to\nthe person being searched; and\n(d) must not be conducted in the presence or view of a person\nwhose presence is not necessary for the purposes of the\nsearch; and\n(e) must not be conducted on a person who is under 10; and\n(f) if the person being searched is at least 10 but under 18, or is\nincapable of managing his or her affairs:\n(i) may only be conducted if a court orders that it be\nconducted; and\n(ii) must be conducted in the presence of a parent or\nguardian of the person being searched or, if that is not\nacceptable to the person, in the presence of another\nperson (other than a police officer) who is capable of\nrepresenting the interests of the person and who, as far\nas is practicable in the circumstances, is acceptable to\nthe person; and\n(g) must not involve a search of a person’s body cavities; and\n(h) must not involve the removal of more garments than the\npolice officer conducting the search believes on reasonable\ngrounds to be necessary to determine whether the person has\nin his or her possession the item searched for or to establish\nthe person’s involvement in the Tribunal offence to which\nthe person’s custody relates; and"
    },
