    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-74",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "74 Announcement before entry",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-74"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.95",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A police officer must, before any person enters premises under a\nwarrant or to arrest a person:\n(a) announce that he or she is authorised to enter the premises;\nand\n(b) give any person at the premises an opportunity to allow entry\nto the premises.\n(2) A police officer is not required to comply with subsection (1) if he\nor she believes on reasonable grounds that immediate entry to the\npremises is required to ensure:\n(a) the safety of a person (including the police officer); or\n(b) that the effective execution of the warrant or the arrest is not\nfrustrated.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A police officer must, before any person enters premises under a\nwarrant or to arrest a person:\n(a) announce that he or she is authorised to enter the premises;\nand\n(b) give any person at the premises an opportunity to allow entry\nto the premises.\n(2) A police officer is not required to comply with subsection (1) if he\nor she believes on reasonable grounds that immediate entry to the\npremises is required to ensure:\n(a) the safety of a person (including the police officer); or\n(b) that the effective execution of the warrant or the arrest is not\nfrustrated.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-74-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-74-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "27c58008f5b0e4c4b185aa4b7edd72015e997a8cb0f717534d3f191225078d6b"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-74",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "74 Announcement before entry",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 95,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A police officer must, before any person enters premises under a\nwarrant or to arrest a person:\n(a) announce that he or she is authorised to enter the premises;\nand\n(b) give any person at the premises an opportunity to allow entry\nto the premises.\n(2) A police officer is not required to comply with subsection (1) if he\nor she believes on reasonable grounds that immediate entry to the\npremises is required to ensure:\n(a) the safety of a person (including the police officer); or\n(b) that the effective execution of the warrant or the arrest is not\nfrustrated."
    },
