    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-77-ss-5",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "77(5) Retention of things seized",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-77-ss-5"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.96",
      "values:originalText": "(5) The Attorney-General must direct the Commissioner to return the\nthing if:\n(a) the reason for its seizure no longer exists; or\n(b) it is decided that the thing is not to be used in evidence by a\nTribunal or in respect of criminal proceedings in Australia;\nunless the thing is forfeited or forfeitable to the Commonwealth or\nis the subject of a dispute as to ownership.",
      "skos:definition": "(5) The Attorney-General must direct the Commissioner to return the\nthing if:\n(a) the reason for its seizure no longer exists; or\n(b) it is decided that the thing is not to be used in evidence by a\nTribunal or in respect of criminal proceedings in Australia;\nunless the thing is forfeited or forfeitable to the Commonwealth or\nis the subject of a dispute as to ownership.",
      "values:partOf": {
        "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-77"
      },
      "cml:asserts": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-77-ss-5-norm"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-77-ss-5-logic-deontic-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-77-ss-5-logic-alleninterval-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-77-ss-5-logic-ltl-3"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-77-ss-5-logic-deontic-4"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-77-ss-5-logic-deontic-5"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "060320240ed8e6f8fb003966e6b8baf261ca1f1d64dea80924da3967a2912424",
      "skos:note": "Return seized thing if reason for seizure no longer exists or thing is not needed in evidence."
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-77-ss-5",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "77(5) Retention of things seized",
      "values:kind": "subsection",
      "cof:pageNumber": 96,
      "values:originalText": "(5) The Attorney-General must direct the Commissioner to return the\nthing if:\n(a) the reason for its seizure no longer exists; or\n(b) it is decided that the thing is not to be used in evidence by a\nTribunal or in respect of criminal proceedings in Australia;\nunless the thing is forfeited or forfeitable to the Commonwealth or\nis the subject of a dispute as to ownership."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-77-ss-5-norm",
      "@type": "values:Obligation",
