        "@id": "values:State"
      },
      "skos:scopeNote": "borne by: State"
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-78-ss-3-logic-deontic-1",
      "@type": "cml:LogicApplication",
      "cml:modality": {
        "@id": "cml:Deontic"
      },
      "cml:operator": "may",
      "cml:logicSummary": "Permission granted by magistrate.",
      "cml:executionSurface": "modalities::logic::deontic",
      "cml:confidence": {
        "@value": 1.0,
        "@type": "xsd:decimal"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:premiseText": "Magistrate satisfied person has escaped custody.",
      "cml:conclusionText": "Warrant issued for police officer to return person."
    },
    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-79",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "79 Arrest of person released on bail",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-79"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.98",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A police officer may, without warrant, arrest a person who has\nbeen released on bail under this Act if the police officer has\nreasonable grounds for believing that the person has contravened,\nor is about to contravene, a term or condition of a recognisance on\nwhich bail was granted to the person.\n(2) A person arrested under subsection (1) must, as soon as\npracticable, be brought before the court by which the person was\nadmitted to bail.\n80  Aiding persons to escape etc.\nSections 46, 46A, 47A, 47C and 48 of the Crimes Act 1914 have\neffect as if:\n(a) arrest pursuant to this Act were arrest in respect of an offence\nagainst a law of the Commonwealth; and\n(b) custody while in Australia pursuant to this Act were custody\nin respect of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth.\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part 8\n\nSection 81\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nCompilation date: 28/03/2026",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A police officer may, without warrant, arrest a person who has\nbeen released on bail under this Act if the police officer has\nreasonable grounds for believing that the person has contravened,\nor is about to contravene, a term or condition of a recognisance on\nwhich bail was granted to the person.\n(2) A person arrested under subsection (1) must, as soon as\npracticable, be brought before the court by which the person was\nadmitted to bail.\n80  Aiding persons to escape etc.\nSections 46, 46A, 47A, 47C and 48 of the Crimes Act 1914 have\neffect as if:\n(a) arrest pursuant to this Act were arrest in respect of an offence\nagainst a law of the Commonwealth; and\n(b) custody while in Australia pursuant to this Act were custody\nin respect of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth.\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part 8\n\nSection 81\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nCompilation date: 28/03/2026",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-79-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-79-ss-2"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "e1d2b4dbbe4c37dc63b7499338440af368701af46e21f09d345c98515645622e"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-79",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "79 Arrest of person released on bail",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 98,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A police officer may, without warrant, arrest a person who has\nbeen released on bail under this Act if the police officer has\nreasonable grounds for believing that the person has contravened,\nor is about to contravene, a term or condition of a recognisance on\nwhich bail was granted to the person.\n(2) A person arrested under subsection (1) must, as soon as\npracticable, be brought before the court by which the person was\nadmitted to bail.\n80  Aiding persons to escape etc.\nSections 46, 46A, 47A, 47C and 48 of the Crimes Act 1914 have\neffect as if:\n(a) arrest pursuant to this Act were arrest in respect of an offence\nagainst a law of the Commonwealth; and\n(b) custody while in Australia pursuant to this Act were custody\nin respect of an offence against a law of the Commonwealth.\n\n\nMiscellaneous  Part 8\n\nSection 81\nInternational War Crimes Tribunals Act 1995\nCompilation date: 28/03/2026"
    },
    {
