    {
      "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-81",
      "@type": "cml:Concept",
      "skos:prefLabel": "81 Legal assistance",
      "cml:realizedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-81"
      },
      "cml:curationStatus": {
        "@id": "cml:Proposed"
      },
      "cml:schemaVersion": "2",
      "cml:proposedBy": {
        "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/tools/legis2cml"
      },
      "prov:wasDerivedFrom": {
        "@id": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf"
      },
      "dc:source": "international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995.pdf, p.99",
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person who:\n(a) has instituted, or proposes to institute, a proceeding before a\nmagistrate or a court under this Act or in respect of detention\nunder this Act; or\n(b) is, or will be, a party to such a proceeding; or\n(c) is, or will be, giving evidence or producing documents or\nother articles at such a proceeding;\nmay apply to the Attorney-General for assistance under this section\nin respect of the proceeding.\n(2) If the Attorney-General is satisfied that:\n(a) it would involve hardship to the person to refuse the\napplication; and\n(b) in all the circumstances, it is reasonable that the application\nbe granted;\nthe Attorney-General may authorise provision by the\nCommonwealth to the person of such legal or financial assistance\nin relation to the proceeding as the Attorney-General determines.\n(3) The assistance may be granted unconditionally or subject to such\nconditions as the Attorney-General determines.",
      "skos:definition": "(1) A person who:\n(a) has instituted, or proposes to institute, a proceeding before a\nmagistrate or a court under this Act or in respect of detention\nunder this Act; or\n(b) is, or will be, a party to such a proceeding; or\n(c) is, or will be, giving evidence or producing documents or\nother articles at such a proceeding;\nmay apply to the Attorney-General for assistance under this section\nin respect of the proceeding.\n(2) If the Attorney-General is satisfied that:\n(a) it would involve hardship to the person to refuse the\napplication; and\n(b) in all the circumstances, it is reasonable that the application\nbe granted;\nthe Attorney-General may authorise provision by the\nCommonwealth to the person of such legal or financial assistance\nin relation to the proceeding as the Attorney-General determines.\n(3) The assistance may be granted unconditionally or subject to such\nconditions as the Attorney-General determines.",
      "cml:hasPart": [
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-81-ss-1"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-81-ss-2"
        },
        {
          "@id": "concept:international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995-sec-81-ss-3"
        }
      ],
      "cml:integrityHash": "9e9f06c585814de7d91ee6cbe2a7659ef246b887a903a3ce59c6b9117d1630d7"
    },
    {
      "@id": "https://ns.webcivics.net/values/international-war-crimes-tribunals-act-1995#sec-81",
      "@type": "cof:Section",
      "cof:title": "81 Legal assistance",
      "values:kind": "section",
      "cof:pageNumber": 99,
      "values:originalText": "(1) A person who:\n(a) has instituted, or proposes to institute, a proceeding before a\nmagistrate or a court under this Act or in respect of detention\nunder this Act; or\n(b) is, or will be, a party to such a proceeding; or\n(c) is, or will be, giving evidence or producing documents or\nother articles at such a proceeding;\nmay apply to the Attorney-General for assistance under this section\nin respect of the proceeding.\n(2) If the Attorney-General is satisfied that:\n(a) it would involve hardship to the person to refuse the\napplication; and\n(b) in all the circumstances, it is reasonable that the application\nbe granted;\nthe Attorney-General may authorise provision by the\nCommonwealth to the person of such legal or financial assistance\nin relation to the proceeding as the Attorney-General determines.\n(3) The assistance may be granted unconditionally or subject to such\nconditions as the Attorney-General determines."
    },
